{"unit":8,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 8","tracks":{"a87":"Track_8.7.mp3"},"SEGS":{"iceland":["a87",3.92,107.99]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 8 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Happiness and heroes</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 8, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;7. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u8\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">Nobody is asking for luxury. The request is perfectly&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">generous</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">balanced</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">reasonable</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">He never thinks about anybody else. He is completely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">selfish</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">brave</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">content</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">If you know&hellip;, you can help somebody before the ambulance arrives.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">culture shock</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">first aid</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">eye contact</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">Everybody else was in a suit. I turned up in jeans and felt completely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">unrealistic</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">appropriate</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">underdressed</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match each prefix word to what it means. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"h1\">misjudge</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"h2\">overspend</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"h3\">undercook</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"h4\">reschedule</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"h5\">reappear</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"h3\" data-short=\"not cook enough\">not cook it for long enough</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"h5\" data-short=\"come back\">come back after being gone</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"h1\" data-short=\"judge wrongly\">form the wrong opinion of somebody</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"h4\" data-short=\"move to a new time\">move it to a new time</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"h2\" data-short=\"spend too much\">spend more than you should</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with one word from the box: <b>cost &middot; poverty &middot; capable</b>.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">Wages have not moved, but the <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"cost\" data-why=\"The <b>cost</b> of living.\"> of living has risen every year.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">Free childcare and healthcare are the main reason child <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"poverty\" data-why=\"<b>Poverty</b> = being very poor.\"> is low there.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">I honestly do not think I would be <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"capable\" data-why=\"<b>Be capable of</b> doing something.\"> of running into a burning building.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">If it&hellip; tomorrow, we will cancel the walk.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">will rain</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">rains</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">would rain</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">If I&hellip; braver, I would be a firefighter.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">am</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">will be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">were</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">&hellip; the economy grows, wages will not rise at all.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Unless</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">As long as</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">In case</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">What&hellip; if you saw somebody being bullied at work?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">will you do</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">would you do</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">do you do</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Real or unreal? What does each sentence tell you about now?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">If I had time, I would volunteer. <select data-answer=\"U\" data-why=\"An imagined present &rarr; I do not have time.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"R\">there is a real chance of it</option><option value=\"U\">it is not true now</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">If I have time, I will volunteer. <select data-answer=\"R\" data-why=\"A real possibility &rarr; I may well have time.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"R\">there is a real chance of it</option><option value=\"U\">it is not true now</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">If she knew first aid, she could help. <select data-answer=\"U\" data-why=\"She does not know first aid, so she cannot help.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"R\">there is a real chance of it</option><option value=\"U\">it is not true now</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>not / cancel</i>) If it rains, we <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"won't cancel|will not cancel\" data-why=\"The negative goes on <b>will</b>, never on the <i>if</i> clause.\"> the whole day.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>win</i>) If we <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"won\" data-why=\"An imagined situation &rarr; past form after <i>if</i>.\"> the lottery, we would give some of it away.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>land</i>) I will message you as soon as I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"land\" data-why=\"No <i>will</i> after <b>as soon as</b> &mdash; present simple.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">If it <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"rains\" data-why=\"No <b>will</b> after <i>if</i> &mdash; the condition takes the present simple.\">, we’ll stay in.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">You will miss it <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"unless\" data-why=\"<b>Unless</b> already means <i>if not</i>, so a second negative is wrong.\"> you leave now.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">I am not brave, so I am not a firefighter.<br>If I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"were braver, i'd be a firefighter|were braver i would be a firefighter|was braver i'd be a firefighter\" data-why=\"An imagined present &rarr; past form + <b>would</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">My advice: talk to your manager.<br>If I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"were you, i'd talk to your manager|were you i would talk to your manager|were you, i'd talk to him\" data-why=\"<b>If I were you, I&rsquo;d&hellip;</b> &mdash; always <i>were</i>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The town that gave everybody money</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">For two years, two thousand people in Finland were paid the same amount every month, whether they worked or not. The result surprised almost everybody.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>The design was simple. Two thousand unemployed people, chosen at random, received 560 euros a month for two years. They kept it if they found work. Nobody had to prove anything, attend anything or explain anything. If the scheme worked, the researchers expected two results: people would find jobs faster, and they would say they felt better.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>Only one of those happened. The employment effect was small &mdash; a few days more work per year than the control group, which is not nothing, but it is not what supporters had promised either. What was not small was the second result. People in the scheme reported markedly less stress, better health and far more trust in other people and in institutions. If you had asked them which mattered more, most would have said the second.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>Critics were quick to point out that this is exactly what an expensive experiment ought to be judged on: if a country pays everybody and unemployment barely moves, the policy has failed on its own terms. Supporters answered that the terms were wrong. A society that is less anxious is not a side effect, they argued; it is the point, and the fact that nobody knows how to put a price on it does not make it worthless.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>The Finnish government did not continue the scheme. Yet the argument it started has not stopped, partly because the researchers were honest about what they had and had not shown. Two years is short. Two thousand people is few. Unless a study runs long enough for people to make real decisions &mdash; to retrain, to move, to start something &mdash; it cannot tell you what a permanent version would do. That study has still not been run anywhere.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">What did the researchers expect to find?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">that people would stop looking for work</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">that people would find jobs faster and feel better</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">that the cost would fall over two years</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">What was the clearest result of the experiment?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">a large rise in employment</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">a fall in the cost of living</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">a marked improvement in how people felt</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">People lost the money if they found a job. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph A: they <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">The participants were chosen at random. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A says so directly.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">Other countries have since copied the scheme. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text never says what other countries did.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The government continued the scheme after two years. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: the government <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, what do supporters mean by saying &ldquo;the terms were wrong&rdquo;?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the experiment was being judged on the wrong measure</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the payment was too small</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the participants had been badly chosen</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">Why does the writer say the argument has not stopped?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">because the government refused to publish the results</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">because the researchers admitted what the study could not show</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">because the participants complained</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('iceland',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> The life you would choose &middot; three years in Iceland\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 8.7</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word or a number.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">Babies are left to sleep outside cafés in their <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"prams|pram\" data-why=\"They sleep outside in their <b>prams</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">Nobody worries, because crime rates are very <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"low\" data-why=\"Crime rates are very <b>low</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">One in <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"10|ten\" data-why=\"One in <b>ten</b> Icelanders is said to be a published author.\"> Icelanders is said to be a published author.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;At first this used to drive me mad.&rdquo; Her first reaction to Icelandic timekeeping was\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">amusement</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">indifference</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">irritation</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Why does she mention that one in ten Icelanders is a published author?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">to show that the relaxed school system still produces educated people</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">to say that books there are cheap</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">to explain why she moved</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">Her attitude to Iceland now is best described as\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">homesick</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">settled and fond of it</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">undecided</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You are announcing the plan of a three-minute talk.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">To sum up, there are three things.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Today I am going to look at three things.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Are there any questions?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You are leaving one point and starting the next.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Thank you for listening.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">First of all, a little background.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Now, let us move on to why it happens.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You want to turn a statistic into its consequence.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">What this means in practice is that&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Let me give you an example.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Moving on&hellip;</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Good note, or bad note? Sort each one.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Good\">meetings 11 hrs/wk, 4 useful</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Bad\">The average person in this office sat in eleven hours of meetings every week</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Good\">cause = politeness, not necessity</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Bad\">meetings</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Good\"><h5>A good note</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Bad\"><h5>Too long, or too vague</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the talk in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"t3,t1,t4,t2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"t1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">In today&rsquo;s talk I am going to look at three things.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"t2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">To sum up: we lose seven hours a week each, and we lose it out of politeness. Thank you for listening.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"t3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Good morning. My name is Aigerim, and I am here to talk to you about the meeting nobody needed.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"t4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">So, how much time do we lose? We counted for six weeks.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Bota</b>They are publishing the happiness report in May.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>If we <select data-answer=\"come\" data-why=\"Present simple after <i>come</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>will come</option><option>came</option><option>come</option></select> in the top twenty, I will be amazed.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Bota</b>We will not, <select data-answer=\"unless\" data-why=\"<b>unless</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>unless</option><option>as long as</option><option>in case</option></select> the cost of living comes down first.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>True. If I <select data-answer=\"were\" data-why=\"An imagined present &rarr; <b>were</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am</option><option>were</option><option>will be</option></select> the minister, I would start with childcare.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Bota</b>Would that really change anything?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Denmark says so. And if I <select data-answer=\"had to\" data-why=\"Unreal condition &rarr; past form.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>have to</option><option>had to</option><option>would have to</option></select> give one figure, it would be the trust one. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> There <select data-answer=\"has been\" data-why=\"From the past up to now &rarr; present perfect. <b>has been</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>has been</option><option>is being</option><option>was</option></select> a steady increase in it since 2012.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Bota</b>Where did you read all this?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>A talk last week. <select data-answer=\"What made you ask\" data-why=\"A subject question &mdash; no <i>What made you ask</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>What did make you ask</option><option>What you made ask</option><option>What made you ask</option></select>?</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 120&ndash;140 words. Give yourself twenty-five minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write the notes and then the opening of a three-minute talk on this question: <i>what one change would make people in your city happier?</i> Start with the notes &mdash; no more than eight words in total. Then write the first two paragraphs of the talk from those notes: who you are and what the talk is about, the plan, and your first point with one number in it.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"NOTES:&#10;&#10;TALK:  Good morning. I am here to talk to you about&hellip;   In today&rsquo;s talk I am going to look at&hellip;   First of all&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your talk must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>notes of <b>eight words or fewer</b>, using numbers, arrows and abbreviations</li>\n        <li>an opening that names you and the subject</li>\n        <li>a plan announced before the first point</li>\n        <li>one number, and one sentence beginning <b>What this means in practice is&hellip;</b></li>\n        <li>one conditional: <b>If we&hellip;, we will&hellip;</b> or <b>If we&hellip;, we would&hellip;</b></li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; three minutes, from notes only</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Give the whole three-minute talk from your eight words of notes. Do not read the written version. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>what would you do if you saw somebody in real danger?</i> Say what most people would do, what you would do, and what you would advise a friend to do.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>open, announce the plan, land one point with a number, close</li>\n        <li>at least one real conditional and one unreal conditional, correctly distinguished</li>\n        <li><b>If I were you, I would&hellip;</b> once, for the advice</li>\n        <li>no <i>will</i> and no <i>would</i> after <i>if</i></li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>I am here to talk to you about&hellip; &middot; First of all&hellip; &middot; What this means in practice is&hellip; &middot; To sum up&hellip; &middot; If we do X, we will&hellip; &middot; If I saw&hellip;, I would&hellip; &middot; If I were you&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my notes are eight words or fewer and I could still speak from them</li>\n        <li>I announced the plan before the first point</li>\n        <li>I gave at least one number the audience could hold on to</li>\n        <li>I closed the talk instead of simply stopping</li>\n        <li>I gave the talk without reading the written version</li>\n        <li>my real and unreal conditionals said different things about now</li>\n        <li>no <i>will</i> and no <i>would</i> appeared after <i>if</i></li>\n        <li>I used <i>If I were you, I would&hellip;</i> for the advice</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}